      Shrimp & Corn Chowder - Ladies Home Journal Feb 06 p.194

      30 minutes prep, 75 minutes total time (good luck)

      4 T    butter
      1.5    lbs medium shrimp peeled & deveined
      2.75   white onions, chopped
      3 T    garlic, chopped
      1 c    sweetish white wine (Riesling, saki?)
      2 c    poblano peppers, roasted, peeled, seeded, chopped
      1/2 t  ground cumin
      3/4 lb yukon gold potatoes peeled & quartered
      3/4 lb red potatoes peeled & cut bite-size
      3 c    corn kernels (frozen OK.  fresh better)
      1 c    half&half
      1/4 c  cilantro, chopped

      Melt 2 T butter in 5 qt pot.  Add shrimp shells, 1/2 the
      onion, 1/2 the garlic.  Cook with stirring till shells
      turn bright pink with some brown edges.  About 4 minutes.

      Add wine & 4 cups water, simmer till reduced to 4 cups 
      total.  About 20 minutes.  Strain stock & wipe out pot.

      Melt 2 T butter, add rest of onion, cumin, peppers and
      cook till onion is tender - about 3 minutes.  Add rest of
      garlic, cook 1 minute.  Add stock & potatoes and cook till
      potatoes tender - about 20 minutes.  Remove most of Yukon
      gold (bigger pieces) and mash and return to pot.

      Add corn, let chowder come back to simmer.  Add shrimp and
      cook just until shrimp are done (use color coded shrimp).

      Add half&half and serve, garnished with cilantro.

